EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
       The program below optionally makes use of pptthhrreeaadd__aattttrr__iinniitt() and
       various related functions to initialize a thread attributes object that
       is used to create a single thread.  Once created, the thread uses the
       pptthhrreeaadd__ggeettaattttrr__nnpp(3) function (a nonstandard GNU extension) to
       retrieve the thread’s attributes, and then displays those attributes.

       If the program is run with no command‐line argument, then it passes
       NULL as the _a_t_t_r argument of pptthhrreeaadd__ccrreeaattee(3), so that the thread is
       created with default attributes.  Running the program on Linux/x86‐32
       with the NPTL threading implementation, we see the following:

           $ uulliimmiitt --ss       # No stack limit ==> default stack size is 2 MB
           unlimited
           $ ..//aa..oouutt
           Thread attributes:
                   Detach state        = PTHREAD_CREATE_JOINABLE
                   Scope               = PTHREAD_SCOPE_SYSTEM
                   Inherit scheduler   = PTHREAD_INHERIT_SCHED
                   Scheduling policy   = SCHED_OTHER
                   Scheduling priority = 0
                   Guard size          = 4096 bytes
                   Stack address       = 0x40196000
                   Stack size          = 0x201000 bytes

       When we supply a stack size as a command‐line argument, the program
       initializes a thread attributes object, sets various attributes in that
       object, and passes a pointer to the object in the call to
       pptthhrreeaadd__ccrreeaattee(3).  Running the program on Linux/x86‐32 with the NPTL
       threading implementation, we see the following:

           $ ..//aa..oouutt 00xx33000000000000
           posix_memalign() allocated at 0x40197000
           Thread attributes:
                   Detach state        = PTHREAD_CREATE_DETACHED
                   Scope               = PTHREAD_SCOPE_SYSTEM
                   Inherit scheduler   = PTHREAD_EXPLICIT_SCHED
                   Scheduling policy   = SCHED_OTHER
                   Scheduling priority = 0
                   Guard size          = 0 bytes
                   Stack address       = 0x40197000
                   Stack size          = 0x3000000 bytes

